  "definition": {
    "withheld": "A forward-only member receives a grafted snapshot of the tip, so it sees every blob and path reachable from HEAD. What the window withholds is the complement: superseded blob versions and paths deleted before the join epoch.",
    "not_withheld": "Current code, current secrets, and the present directory structure are all disclosed by the grafted snapshot. A history window bounds historical exposure, not present exposure."
  },
